fe.append_section(S, '03', '## One gate per rule', """Before the fix pass `validateCourse` had two layers: the new type gate (`isText`, `whole`) and, below it, the original string and number checks that could no longer be reached. Two layers for one rule are a maintenance hazard: a future edit to the lower one silently does nothing, and a reader cannot tell which message a client will see. The rule now: each input rule has exactly one gate, and the cross-field rule `enrolled <= capacity` (which pre-dates the change) is the only check after normalization. Note also what the change did *not* add: `enrolled <= capacity` already existed; the change added the type gate, the normalized-code uniqueness (409) and the level vocabulary in front of it.""", before='## How to reason through the code')
